# Testing (AUnit)

**Every implemented feature must have tests.** Use **AUnit** ([AdaCore/aunit](https://github.com/AdaCore/aunit)) for all Ada tests. This is an allowed third-party library.

- Add tests in the same change as the feature; do not ship untested compiler/JIT/LIR/CLI/`tooling`/`hypatia`/`alexandria`/`format` behavior.
- Prefer AUnit fixtures/test cases over ad-hoc `Put_Line` drivers. `samples/` are extra, not a substitute for unit tests.
- Host tests live in a **nested Alire crate** (`<folder>/tests`, own `alire.toml`, pin `{ path = ".." }`, crate name `lovelace_<component>_tests`). Declare AUnit **only** there, not on the library or `lovelace` crates. Host test crates `with` `shared/lovelace_host_switches.gpr`.
- Host crates (full RTS): AUnit with file I/O is fine.
- Freestanding/native Augusta Ada: AUnit is designed for **ZFP**. In that code, do **not** use containers, finalization, or exception propagation even in tests. Honor AUnit `FileIO` vs `nofileio` as needed.

Do not pull other test frameworks (VUnit, Python pytest for Ada units, etc.) unless the user asks.